%% AWS Fullstack Template — One streamed agent turn, end to end
%% Import into Lucidchart: File > Import Diagram > Mermaid.
%% This is the path that crosses every layer, so it is the best single
%% picture of how the layers actually relate at runtime.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant B as Browser SPA
    participant CF as CloudFront
    participant ALB as Internal ALB
    participant R as Router L2
    participant S as chat_service L2
    participant D as session_repository L3
    participant RT as runtime.py L4
    participant HC as client.py L4
    participant H as AgentCore Harness
    participant M as Managed memory

    Note over B,M: Precondition — the session already exists and its runtime config was frozen at creation

    B->>CF: POST /api/v1/sessions/{id}/messages<br/>body {"message":"..."}<br/>Authorization Bearer app JWT
    Note right of B: The ONLY things the browser sends:<br/>message text and an opaque session id
    CF->>ALB: behavior /api/* — uncached, forwards viewer request
    ALB->>R: HTTP :8000

    R->>R: verify app JWT, extract owner from sub
    R->>S: handle_message(owner, session_id, text)

    S->>D: get(owner_id, session_id)
    D-->>S: session row or key miss
    Note over S,D: Ownership is the partition key.<br/>Missing and foreign both return 404 —<br/>the client cannot tell them apart.

    S->>RT: load frozen snapshot
    RT-->>S: resolved config — model, tool refs, system prompt, memory_ref
    Note over RT: Nothing is re-resolved here.<br/>Later edits to the source config<br/>cannot reach a live session.

    S->>HC: invoke(harness_arn, config, memory_ref, text)
    HC->>H: streaming invoke

    Note over HC: Bridge — the SDK iterator blocks,<br/>SSE needs async. Worker thread + queue,<br/>request id rebound inside the thread.

    H-->>HC: text chunk
    HC-->>R: chunk
    R-->>B: SSE delta

    H-->>HC: tool call request
    HC-->>R: chunk
    R-->>B: SSE tool_started
    HC->>HC: dispatch to local Python function<br/>via TOOL_DISPATCH
    R-->>B: SSE tool_input
    HC->>H: tool result
    R-->>B: SSE tool_finished
    Note over HC,H: A failing or unknown tool becomes a tool<br/>RESULT the model can explain or route around,<br/>never an exception that ends the turn.

    H-->>HC: text chunk
    R-->>B: SSE delta

    H->>M: append the turn's events
    Note over M: Managed memory owns conversation content.<br/>DynamoDB never stores it.

    H-->>HC: end of stream
    R-->>B: SSE done

    alt failure mid-stream
        H-->>HC: botocore error
        HC->>HC: classify — dependency_category + retryable<br/>log the original against the request id
        R-->>B: SSE error {code, retryable, requestId}
        Note over B: Partial text already streamed is PRESERVED.<br/>A dropped connection never erases a partial answer.<br/>The HTTP status went out with the first byte,<br/>so the taxonomy has to travel in the body.
    end
